## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; a shape is graded by it wherever it appears; capability decides, the refusal-set comparison only finds candidates)
- **G-1 head allows what `c7365aee`/base refused, or base answered 5xx and head answers 2xx:** the end state is one that base stores through a request base ALLOWS (replayed at base) = Note/FACT by shape; any case base cannot reach = **Blocker**; not yet proven reachable at the verdict is graded unreachable (Blocker); say proven / not proven counts.
- **G-2 head refuses what base stored/answered 2xx:** expected for the named shapes; a refusal of any input a LEGITIMATE client sends (every body the existing suite and the web's fixtures send, every enum member name, a name written with JSON escapes, a 1-40 identifier member that the contract has) = **Major**; stricter outside the named shapes = **Minor** (named). B538-8 (other-case enum spellings, kept by the B518 scope) = Note, as ruled; the care-SKU blank/whitespace restore is the one allowed widening back to base.
- **G-3 head answers 5xx on a hostile body or store** on the quote routes and the store-load routes: **Major**; a 5xx that stored something first = **Major** whatever the route; on a route/shape outside the seven items and equal at base = **Note/FACT with the capability stated** (who can cause it, what it takes down). A null `tierPool` (fix STATUS FOR TUESDAY 4) is graded here, C5.
- **G-4 a message or body leak** in a 4xx/5xx of the quote routes: a .NET type name, byte position, `LineNumber`, `Path:`, stack, file path, row value or internal figure = **Major**; an echo of caller-sent text: a name the contract HAS in the caller's case or an array index = **Note**; any other caller-chosen text (a member name that is not a 1-40 `[A-Za-z0-9_]` identifier, a key, a section id) = **Major if unbounded, if it carries CR/LF/control characters or non-ASCII, or if it defeats the stated rule "no caller-chosen name is printed unless it is a 1-40 identifier"**, else Minor. The detail bound of the fix seat is 200 characters; the 400 body bound 4,096 bytes for the null-entry class.
- **G-5 a restricted caller reads more at the head than at base:** Blocker if an internal figure/method base hid; Major if it only reveals that an internal input exists; Note if base showed the same (differential by caller shape).
- **G-6 a surviving mutant** on a check that decides what is stored, a refusal of hostile input, a size or count bound, the store-load fault mapping, or the shape of a result: **Major**, unless a FORCED RUN shows it unreachable through every input path your census found (then **Minor**, census and run attached). Any other survivor: Minor unless proven equivalent. **One exception, ruled in B543:** the early-stop-versus-truncate-after-walk mutant of the null cap (`N3d` of the fix STATUS) changes time, not state: it is accepted as killed BY MEASUREMENT if YOU reproduce the time ratio (fix STATUS: 5.9M nulls 160-243 ms at the fix vs 997-1,216 ms under the mutant) in a held slot with load1 recorded; if your ratio is under 2x, report it as a Minor with your figures.
- **G-7 a stored document the head cannot read back** (a quote, snapshot, store file base read with 200): **Major**, except a document holding one of the named shapes (Note, with its count). A store file base served (an empty or blank care SKU) must read 200 again.
- **G-8 CI.** A failing check-run on the head or the merge result = **Major**; a check `in_progress` at the verdict: the verdict line says `CI pending: <names>` and is at most GO WITH FINDINGS; a missing analysis is NOT scanned, never clean; a new open alert on the PR ref = **Blocker**.
- **G-9 words.** A user/API-consumer-visible string in the delta missing from the WORDS-DRAFT table = **Major** (one finding per string); a table row whose text or `file:line` disagrees with the head = **Minor**; the ONE pending sentence is expected, is NOT a finding, and is not approved or judged by the gate (the product owner's). The gate does not approve words.
- **G-10 growing answers and worker time.** A request within the accepted body size whose 4xx body or worker time grows with the request and reaches megabytes or seconds = **Major** when the lines were added or changed by this PR (the 13 commits); for lines this PR does not touch and base has equally = **Note/FACT with your measured growth**, listed as an open instance for Tuesday to ticket (the cap: a new class is not found at round 2 without being ticketed).
- **Always Blocker:** a path beyond the 20, a change to `.github/`, `docs/`, `web/`, a `.csproj`, `ApiJson.cs`, `PurchaseCalculator.cs`, a fenced file; a secret or customer datum in an added line; the head moved; a person's name in an added line or message. **Always Major:** an existing test removed, skipped, loosened or edited beyond the stated lines; a name lost or one added beyond the 103; a test red at the head and green at `c7365aee` other than a row pinning a ruled new behaviour; a build warning; a fix-seat claim your measurement contradicts (20 paths, 13 commits, 103 names, Api 2,316 / Engine 400 / Import 156 on the branch's own tree, 87 mutant records, unexplained differential 0); a ticket key, decision-card id, finding id or percent figure in code or a commit. **Always Note:** the squash artefact, CI pending at the verdict (stated), the fix seat's process disclosures (an `rm -f` of its own scratch file, a first mutant launch that ran 0 rows), style.

## LOAD (binding; the MPS heavy-slot convention, RELAYED from B538 and B547)
8 cores. Heavy = `dotnet build`, `dotnet test`, `dotnet test --list-tests`, `npm ci`, `npm test`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build`, a mutant matrix, a corpus replay at two trees, the full CI line. **Start a heavy run only while `uptime` load1 is below 8** at two reads 4 s apart (not independent: say so), recorded beside the result; at 8 or over poll every 20 s, log each wait, and do the light work meanwhile (C1, C2 reading, C7, C9, C10 by GitHub, the corpus and oracle design). **Then take ONE slot atomically:** `mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-1' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-2' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-3'`, write `B552 <start time> <label>` into its `holder`; read every other holder first (measured: slot 2 held by B550; a holder that looks stale is reported, never removed). All taken: wait 3 minutes and retry. At most ONE slot, one heavy job at a time; **re-read load1 at the start of EACH job inside a held slot** (the fix seat ran its mutant battery at load1 up to 13.8: do not repeat that; its per-mutant load1 is in its table); at the run's end remove ONLY your own slot. The shared `.tools/.git-lock` wraps GIT REF WRITES ONLY (`fetch`, `worktree add`). Write your OWN wrapper in `.tools/b552/`. Never kill a process by name. NO artificial load. The SDK is project-local `<project root>/.tools/dotnet`, run with `-nodeReuse:false -p:UseSharedCompilation=false` and `DOTNET_CLI_USE_MSBUILD_SERVER=0`; record `node --version`, `npm --version` (CI uses node 24; the fix seat used v26.8.1; `web/package.json` engines accept >= 20.19.0). **The web tree is byte-equal to base (0 `web/` paths): run the web line once and say it proves nothing beyond the PR's own web check.**

